/* SGU Go: English narration from content/poi-descriptions.csv (prepared by Nhung).
   Sets dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION.translated_text (lang = 'en') to the text read in content/audio/poi-XX.mp3,
   so the text-to-speech fallback says the same thing as the audio file. Safe to run more than once. */
USE [SGUGo];
GO

UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'Welcome to the main building of Saigon University, Building C, on the main campus at 273 An Duong Vuong Street. The campus has its roots in a French-Chinese school founded in 1908, later known as the Bac Ai Institute. Its architecture blends French and Chinese influences, and one of the campus buildings, nearly one hundred and twenty years old, has been recognized as an architectural and artistic heritage site. Saigon University itself was established in 2007, building on the teacher-training tradition of the Ho Chi Minh City College of Pedagogy, founded in 1976. Take a moment to look at the facade before you continue your visit.' WHERE poi_id = 1 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is KLF, part of the Learning Resource Center, the university''s library. The reference room is on the first floor, and the reading room is on the second floor. The library also has lending rooms where students can borrow printed materials. The center began opening on Saturdays in September 2019, which makes it a useful place to study at the weekend, but opening hours can change, so please check the library website before your visit. As in any library, please keep your voice low and your phone on silent.' WHERE poi_id = 2 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at the volleyball court on the main campus of Saigon University. Together with the football field and the multipurpose hall, it is one of the places where students exercise and play sports between classes. The main campus stands on An Duong Vuong Street, in the part of Ho Chi Minh City long known as Cholon. Saigon University was established in 2007 and grew out of the city''s teacher-training tradition. If a class or a team is practicing, please give way and stay clear of the court.' WHERE poi_id = 5 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at the canteen on the main campus, where students and staff take a break and have a meal between classes. Saigon University is a public university under the Ho Chi Minh City People''s Committee. Besides this main campus on An Duong Vuong Street, it has Campus 1 on Ba Huyen Thanh Quan Street and Campus 2 on Ton Duc Thang Street. Menus, prices and serving hours may change, so please check at the counter. Please keep the tables tidy so the next visitors can sit down comfortably.' WHERE poi_id = 6 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Block B on the main campus. The main campus brings together many of the university''s faculties, administrative departments and learning centers, including faculties such as Law, Foreign Languages, Information Technology, and Culture and Tourism. Because the campus has several blocks, the easiest way to find a classroom or an office is to check the directory near the entrance and the room number on your schedule. If you are a visitor, please ask the staff for directions.' WHERE poi_id = 7 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are near the Office of Testing and Educational Quality Assurance. As its name says, this unit takes care of organizing examinations and of quality assurance in teaching and learning at the university. Quality matters to every university, because it shows how well teaching, testing and student services meet the standards they set for themselves. If you have a question about exams or assessment, please check the university''s announcements first, and confirm the office''s working hours before you come.' WHERE poi_id = 8 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at the football field on the main campus. It is an open space for sports and recreation, and a good place to see student life in action. The story of Saigon University began far from here. In 1972, a secondary teacher-training school was founded in War Zone C, in Tay Ninh province. After 1975 it moved to Saigon, became the Ho Chi Minh City College of Pedagogy in 1976, and was upgraded to Saigon University in 2007. If a match or practice is in progress, please watch your step and stay off the pitch.' WHERE poi_id = 9 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is the basketball court in the multipurpose hall on the main campus. Because it is indoors, students can practice and play here whatever the weather. The hall also hosts other sports, including badminton and table tennis, which you will find at the next stops. The university''s other two city campuses are on Ba Huyen Thanh Quan Street and Ton Duc Thang Street. Please check the schedule before you enter, and give way to classes and teams that are practicing.' WHERE poi_id = 10 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is the badminton area in the multipurpose hall. Badminton is one of the most popular sports among students in Vietnam, and an indoor hall means that play is not interrupted by sun or rain. Saigon University was established in 2007, and today its students come from many faculties, from education and languages to law and technology. Please follow the court markings, and check the usage information posted at the venue before you play.' WHERE poi_id = 11 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is the table tennis area in the multipurpose hall. It is a place for a quick game between classes or a friendly match with classmates. The university is run under the Ho Chi Minh City People''s Committee, and facilities like this are shared by students from every faculty. Please handle the tables and any shared equipment with care, and follow the facility rules posted in the hall, so everyone can enjoy a game.' WHERE poi_id = 12 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at Building E on the main campus. The main campus is home to the offices of many faculties, including Information Technology, Law, Foreign Languages, Mathematics and Applications, and Education. To find the classroom or area you are looking for, check the floor directory and the room numbers, or ask a member of staff for guidance. The main campus covers a large part of the university, which together with its other campuses occupies roughly fifty-seven to sixty thousand square meters in the city center.' WHERE poi_id = 13 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Building A on the main campus of Saigon University. The ground you are standing on has a long educational history. A French-Chinese school opened here in 1908, and after 1975 the site became home to a teacher-training college, which grew into Saigon University in 2007. To find your destination, check the floor directory and room numbers, or ask the staff for help.' WHERE poi_id = 14 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Auditorium A, a venue for university programs, conferences and events. Events such as welcome ceremonies, academic seminars and student activities are usually held in halls like this one. The university has a long tradition: it traces its origins to a teacher-training school founded in 1972 and became Saigon University in 2007. If you are here for an event, please check the event notice for the start time, the correct entrance and the seating arrangements.' WHERE poi_id = 15 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at Self-Study Area 1 on the main campus. It is a space for individual study and group work, so you will often see students reviewing lessons, preparing presentations or working on projects together. If you need books or reference materials, the Learning Resource Center, known as KLF, has a reference room on the first floor and a reading room on the second floor. Here, please keep your voice low, keep the area clean, and follow the rules posted at the entrance.' WHERE poi_id = 16 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Self-Study Area 2 on the main campus. You can use it to review your lessons, prepare for exams or work with classmates. Saigon University is a public university, and spaces like this are shared by students from many different faculties, so a little courtesy goes a long way. Please take care of the furniture and the shared space, keep conversations quiet, and leave the area tidy when you go.' WHERE poi_id = 17 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at Auditorium C on the main campus, a venue for meetings, university programs and campus activities. Over the years, Saigon University has grown from a teacher-training school founded in 1972 into a multi-disciplinary public university, and halls like this one host the ceremonies and gatherings that mark that journey. Before you go in, please check the notice board at the entrance for the schedule and any guidance for visitors.' WHERE poi_id = 18 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Auditorium B on the main campus. It is used for university events, seminars and student programs. Saigon University was formally established on the twenty-fifth of April, 2007, when the Ho Chi Minh City College of Pedagogy was upgraded to a university. If you are attending an event, please check the notice at the entrance for the start time and the correct entry area, and arrive a little early.' WHERE poi_id = 19 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at the Administration Building, marked H B on the campus map. In Vietnamese universities, the word Hieu Bo refers to the administrative block, where the leadership and general administration are based. Saigon University operates under the Ho Chi Minh City People''s Committee and is overseen by the Ministry of Education and Training. If you are visiting on business, please read the guidance board and follow the instructions at the entrance, so the staff can direct you to the right office.' WHERE poi_id = 20 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Building D on the main campus, and it is an important academic building. According to the university''s student affairs listing, it houses the offices of many faculties, including Information Technology, Law, Foreign Languages, Mathematics and Applications, Culture and Tourism, and Primary Education. Use the building sign, the floor directory and the room numbers to find your destination, then continue your visit with the campus map.' WHERE poi_id = 21 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at Building A on Campus 1, at 105 Ba Huyen Thanh Quan Street. This campus is home to the Faculty of Business Administration and the Faculty of Finance and Accounting, whose offices are located in this building. It is one of the university''s three campuses in the city center, together with the main campus on An Duong Vuong Street and Campus 2 on Ton Duc Thang Street. Check the directory and room numbers to find the classroom or office you need.' WHERE poi_id = 22 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is the study area on Campus 1. Campus 1 is home to the Faculty of Business Administration and the Faculty of Finance and Accounting, and a quiet room like this is a good place for preparing reports, practicing presentations or reviewing for exams. You can focus on your own work or study with classmates. Please keep the area quiet, take your belongings with you when you leave, and follow the rules posted in the room.' WHERE poi_id = 23 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Building B on Campus 1. Saigon University has several campuses in the city center, and each one has its own character. Campus 1, on Ba Huyen Thanh Quan Street, is home to the business and finance faculties. Check the room numbers and the signs along the corridors to find the classroom or office you are looking for. If you cannot find it, the staff at the entrance will be happy to help.' WHERE poi_id = 24 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Building C on Campus 1. Campus 1 is one of the university''s campuses in the city center, together with the main campus and Campus 2. Please check the building sign and the floor directory to find your classroom before you move on, and take care in the corridors during class changes, when they can get crowded. Saigon University has been a public university since 2007, with roots in teacher training that go back to 1972.' WHERE poi_id = 25 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at the canteen on Campus 1. You can stop here for a meal or a short break between classes. The campus is at 105 Ba Huyen Thanh Quan Street. Menus and prices vary, so please check the service hours and the menu at the counter. Please keep the tables tidy so the next visitors can sit down comfortably. Campus 1 is also home to the Faculty of Business Administration and the Faculty of Finance and Accounting, so you may meet many of their students here at lunchtime.' WHERE poi_id = 26 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Building B on Campus 2, at 4 Ton Duc Thang Street, close to the Saigon River in the historic center of the city. Campus 2 is home to the Faculty of Preschool Education, which trains teachers for the youngest learners. Use the building signs and the directory to find the classroom or office you need. If you are not sure where to go, please ask the staff at the entrance for directions.' WHERE poi_id = 27 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'You are at Building A on Campus 2. This building houses the offices of the Faculty of Preschool Education, which prepares future teachers for kindergartens and early childhood programs. It continues the tradition that began in 1972, when Saigon University''s earliest predecessor was founded to train teachers. Check the room numbers and signs to find the right route to your destination.' WHERE poi_id = 28 AND lang = N'en';
UPDATE dbo.POI_LOCALIZATION SET translated_text = N'This is Building C on Campus 2. Campus 2 is the university''s campus on Ton Duc Thang Street, a short walk from the Saigon River. Along with the main campus and Campus 1, it is part of Saigon University''s presence in the center of Ho Chi Minh City. Check the directory in this area to find the classroom or university office you want to visit, and keep the walkways clear for people heading to class.' WHERE poi_id = 29 AND lang = N'en';
GO
